<title>CANADA: WIC sets C$150 mln private debt deal.</title>
<headline>WIC sets C$150 mln private debt deal.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Broadcaster WIC Western International Communications Ltd said Thursday it completed a C$150 million private placement of senior notes to U.S. and Canadian institutional investors led by a subsidiary of American General Corp.</p>
<p>The notes have an effective interest rate of approximately 8.4 percent and are due October 11, 2006. TD Securities Inc. was the lead agent for the deal. The company said it was pleased by strong interest from investors and current low interest rates.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314</p>
</text>
